course: dictionary
lesson: 6941
title: Painfully: hurt or very
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Painfully» is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens. It has two meanings. The first is literal: something is done in a way that hurts, like «he walked painfully» on a sprained ankle.
explain: The second meaning is very common in stories and everyday talk. It means very, so much that it feels uncomfortable: «painfully slow», «painfully shy». The word after painfully is the key, and painfully just makes it stronger.
explain: Use the context to choose the meaning. «Soil grows painfully slowly: a few centimetres can take hundreds to a thousand years.» The clue is slowly. Soil cannot feel pain, so painfully means very here. Swap in very: very slowly still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Painfully is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens.
fact: «Painfully» means in a way that hurts or causes pain.
fact: «Painfully» can also mean very, so much that it is uncomfortable: «painfully slow», «painfully shy».
fact: «Painfully obvious» means extremely obvious, often in an embarrassing way.
fact: Soil grows painfully slowly: «a few centimetres can take hundreds to a thousand years».
exercise: «Soil grows painfully slowly: a few centimetres can take hundreds to a thousand years.» What does painfully mean in this sentence? | In a way that hurts someone | Quickly and happily | *Very, so slow that it is uncomfortable | Only just
exercise: Jada says, «The answer was painfully obvious.» What does painfully obvious mean? | *Extremely obvious, often in an embarrassing way | Hurt and bruised | Hard to see at all | Written in pencil
exercise: «He walked painfully after falling off his bike.» What does painfully mean here? | *In a way that hurts, because he is injured | Happily, with a big smile | Sadly, with tears | Very quickly
test: «The little boy was painfully shy at his first party.» What does painfully shy mean? | Loud and bold at parties | Painful to look at | Shy only for a moment | *Very shy, so much that it feels uncomfortable
test: «She was painfully aware that she had forgotten her homework.» What does painfully aware suggest? | Aware only in the morning | Aware of a sore foot | Not aware at all | *Very aware, so it made her feel uncomfortable
exam: Which sentence uses painfully to mean in a way that hurts? | The test was painfully easy | The road was painfully slow | The bus was painfully late | *He hobbled painfully to the door on his sprained ankle
